L66: Figure 2 Squat 1 RM in kilograms for S500 and PLA at week 0 and week 12. Solid bars depict S500 data, while white bars depict PLA data. Data is represented as means ± SD. No difference was found between groups at week 0, and is represented as ‡. A significant group × time interaction ( p  = 0.009) with post hoc tests indicating S500 increased squat 1 RM to a greater extent than PLA.
L67: Figure 3 Bench press 1 RM in kilograms for S500 and PLA at week 0 and week 12. Solid bars depict S500 data, while white bars depict PLA data. Data is represented as means ± SD. No difference was found between groups at week 0 and is represented as ‡. A significant group × time interaction ( p  = 0.048) with post hoc tests indicating S500 increased bench press 1 RM to a greater extent than PLA.
